1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:03,590
How does a parachute turn
a 200 kilometre an hour

2
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:05,590
fall into a gentle landing?

3
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:07,450
It doesn't stop you.

4
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:10,310
It gives the air something
much bigger to push against.

5
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:12,570
Here's what happens, in order.

6
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:16,250
At the right height, a
skydiver throws a small pilot

7
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,170
chute into the wind.

8
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:21,190
It catches the air, pulls
a pin, opens the container

9
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:24,350
on their back, and drags
out a bag with the main

10
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:25,810
parachute folded inside.

11
00:00:26,690 --> 00:00:29,750
The lines stretch out,
the bag lets go, and

12
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,230
the canopy fills with air.

13
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,770
A small square of fabric
called a slider sits on

14
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:38,090
the lines and slows that
opening down, so it doesn't

15
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:39,130
jolt you too hard.

16
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:42,030
And modern canopies
aren't domes.

17
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:46,050
They're wings, made of
cells that fill with air,

18
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:51,090
so a skydiver can steer
and slow right down before

19
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:51,950
touching the ground.

20
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:54,890
Most of the time, it all works.

21
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:58,410
But on roughly one jump
in a thousand, something

22
00:00:58,410 --> 00:00:59,210
goes wrong.

23
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:00,970
The lines can twist.

24
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:05,110
The canopy can open
lopsided, or get stuck in its

25
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:05,910
bag.

26
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:09,230
That's why every skydiver
carries two parachutes.

27
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:12,990
If the main one fails,
they pull one handle to cut

28
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:15,590
it away, and another
to open the reserve.

29
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:19,310
In the US, that reserve has
to be checked and repacked

30
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:23,310
by a certified rigger every
180 days, even if it's

31
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:24,110
never used.

32
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:28,170
And in case a skydiver
can't pull at all, many rigs

33
00:01:28,170 --> 00:01:30,870
carry a small computer
that keeps track of height

34
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:31,670
and speed.

35
00:01:32,410 --> 00:01:34,390
If they're still falling
fast, too close to

36
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:37,930
the ground, it fires and
opens the reserve by itself.

37
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:41,350
So a parachute isn't one
clever piece of fabric.

38
00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:43,610
It's a chain of backups.
